UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p><strong>Gain the forward-thinking practical skills you need to manage teams in the complex, dynamic world of business.&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Griffith''s Bachelor of Business in Management is an online, on-demand degree that gives you the flexibility to learn at your own pace, on your own terms. You''ll build the skills, values and knowledge to thrive in the evolving economy, exploring new approaches to management shaped by innovation and future-focused thinking.&nbsp;</p><p>This degree explores the dynamics of managing people and organisations, focusing on how diverse perspectives and personal attributes shape workplace culture and performance. Integrating concepts from management theory, human resources, organisational behaviour and psychology, you''ll develop the skills to lead effectively, foster collaboration, and build environments where individuals and teams thrive.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Highlights of studying the Bachelor of Business in Management&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>Develop practical leadership and problem-solving skills for managing teams in fast-moving environments across a range of industries.&nbsp;</li><li>Explore how organisations operate in both local and global contexts.&nbsp;</li><li>Build a practical foundation in core business skills for the modern world, guided by the principles of sustainability, inclusiveness and equity.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Stay engaged and on track with access to strong student support, interactive activities and dedicated academic assistance services.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Study 100% online, on demand. Start when you''re ready, set your own pace and pause if you need to.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Combine theory and real-world case studies to build a complete view of modern business strategy.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Graduate ready to lead with confidence, drive innovation and make informed, values-led decisions.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>This degree is part of </strong><a href="https://www.griffith.edu.au/study/griffith-go" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><strong>Griffith GO</strong></a><strong>, our 100% online, on-demand degrees that let you start when you''re ready, study at your own pace and learn from anywhere.&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 156,
    offshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<p>Prerequisites: Nil</p><p>Assumed Knowledge: Any General or Applied English subject (Units 3 &amp; 4, C)</p><p>ATAR/Rank*: 63.00</p><p>VET Qualification: Certificate III</p><p><em>*The above ATAR/Rank from the 2026 admission cycle represents the minimum adjusted ATAR/Rank to which an offer was made. Minimum thresholds can change from year to year and should be used as a guide only for any future intakes.</em></p><p>The University''s <a href="https://sharepointpubstor.blob.core.windows.net/policylibrary-prod/Admission%20Policy.pdf">Admission Policy</a> will apply.</p>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.griffith.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-business-in-management-1719',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '006423F';
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p><strong>Develop the strategic and creative skills essential to thrive in today''s competitive marketing environment.&nbsp;</strong></p><p>In Griffith''s on-demand Bachelor of Business in Marketing, you''ll explore a bold new way of thinking designed for the next generation of marketing professionals. Blending creative strategy with data-driven decision making, this 100% online degree will equip you with the skills, values and knowledge you need for a career in contemporary marketing.&nbsp;</p><p>This degree equips you with the skills to plan and execute impactful campaigns across both established and emerging media platforms. You''ll explore how to attract and retain audiences, strengthen brand presence, and meet strategic objectives in an ever-evolving marketing landscape. From traditional outlets like print, radio, and television to digital spaces such as social media, blogs, and podcasts, you''ll learn how to blend marketing tactics with cutting-edge tools. The course covers essential techniques including search engine optimisation (SEO), search engine marketing (SEM), customer relationship management (CRM), content strategy, brand development, consumer insights, and multi-channel communication, preparing you to thrive in today''s competitive market.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Highlights of studying the Bachelor of Business in Marketing&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>Focus on real, industry-relevant skills in key areas such as strategy, consumer behaviour, branding, digital marketing and market research.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Work on practical projects and case studies that connect theory to industry needs.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Learn to create, communicate and deliver value to customers, preparing you for careers in advertising, public relations, brand management and digital marketing.&nbsp;</li><li>Study 100% online, on demand. Start when you''re ready, set your own pace and pause if you need to.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Build a strong foundation in essential business skills with a focus on sustainability, inclusion and equity while gaining a comprehensive understanding of contemporary marketing strategy.&nbsp;</li><li>Benefit from strong student support, interactive activities and dedicated academic assistance to keep you engaged and motivated.&nbsp;</li><li>Graduate ready to drive innovation and growth through impactful, ethical and customer-focused marketing.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>This degree is part of </strong><a href="https://www.griffith.edu.au/study/griffith-go" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><strong>Griffith GO</strong></a><strong>, our 100% online, on-demand degrees that let you start when you''re ready, study at your own pace and learn from anywhere.&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 156,
    offshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<p>Prerequisites: Nil</p><p>Assumed Knowledge: Any General or Applied English subject (Units 3 &amp; 4, C)</p><p>ATAR/Rank*: 63.00</p><p>VET Qualification: Certificate III</p><p><em>*The above ATAR/Rank from the 2026 admission cycle represents the minimum adjusted ATAR/Rank to which an offer was made. Minimum thresholds can change from year to year and should be used as a guide only for any future intakes.</em></p><p>The University''s <a href="https://sharepointpubstor.blob.core.windows.net/policylibrary-prod/Admission%20Policy.pdf">Admission Policy</a> will apply.</p>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.griffith.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-business-in-marketing-1718',
