UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>Disrupt, innovate and work with industry as you design your way to success. The Bachelor of Design addresses the global need for designers who can navigate the complexities of contemporary society, creatively, ethically and sustainably.</p><p>Our studio-first program, registered by the Design Institute of Australia (DIA), cultivates high levels of design expertise. You''ll learn in innovative, creative studio spaces at the Queensland College of Art and Design and leverage unique opportunities in our world-class facilities, including galleries and purpose-built design studios.</p><h6>Highlights of studying the Bachelor of Design</h6><ul><li>Work with experts from the design industry to tackle real challenges and create innovative solutions.</li><li>Advance your critical and strategic thinking and learn to present your ideas clearly and powerfully.</li><li>Learn from award-winning design professionals and educators, with experience across a wide range of design practices.</li><li>Learn with purpose in this inclusive degree with a focus on making a difference in the field of design and understanding First Nations culture and perspectives.</li><li>Take your learning global with overseas study options that could last a few weeks or even a whole year.</li></ul><h6>Turn your ideas into experience with internships and studio projects&nbsp;</h6><p>You''ll get the chance to do internships and take part in creative studio projects as part of your degree, helping you build your skills and make professional connections.</p><h5>Majors </h5><h6>Visual communication design </h6><p>Explore many different forms of visual and graphic communication and branding and gain a deeper understanding of the social contexts and environmental responsibilities of design. You''ll learn to develop design solutions that inform, persuade, provoke and entertain your audience, as well as how to effectively present and communicate your ideas within this evolving industry.</p><p>In studio classes, you''ll have the creative freedom to explore topics that matter to you and gain industry-informed skills in print media, screen-based interfaces (UI/UX), brand identity, motion, creative entrepreneurship and graphic design solutions.</p><p>LiveWorm-our award-winning design studio-provides an opportunity to kick-start your career by working with real clients and building a professional portfolio under the guidance of experienced teaching staff.</p><p>This major prioritises intercultural perspectives and inclusive world views while building your understanding of our responsibilities as global design citizens.</p><h6>Interior design </h6><p>Prepare to explore diverse spaces and societies, crafting imaginative interiors and public spaces across various scales and domains. With a strong focus on social and environmental justice, sustainability, liveability, diversity and inclusion, this major integrates theory with hands-on practice. Gain a comprehensive toolkit of technical skills, from architectural to digital design programs, while honing your abilities in analysis and critical thinking.</p><p>An emphasis on creativity ensures you''re equipped to tackle complex challenges with innovative and creative solutions, fostering meaningful contributions to the built environment and society at large.</p><h6>Product and user experience design </h6><p>Passionate about using cutting-edge digital technology to design unique products and experiences? This major equips you with hands-on skills in additive manufacturing (3D printing), virtual modelling, simulation, laser cutting and CNC fabrication.</p><p>You''ll learn future-ready skills that combine both the physical and digital worlds, while also evaluating the impact your designs have on people and the environment. You''ll use user-focused design methods and hands-on digital tools to create new products, systems and services that change the way people live in and interact with the world.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 156,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 115500,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Academic entry requirements (by country)</h4><p>Academic entry requirements apply to International applicants for this program. You can view the academic entry requirements for this program <a href="" data-target="#intlEntryModal" data-toggle="modal">here</a>.</p><h5><strong>Inherent requirements</strong></h5><p>Inherent requirements are the essential components of a program or course that demonstrate the abilities, knowledge and skills required to achieve the core learning outcomes of the course or unit.&nbsp;</p><p>Inherent requirements for this program are identified <a href="https://www.griffith.edu.au/__data/assets/pdf_file/0028/2218924/BACHELOR-OF-DESIGN.pdf" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">here</a>.</p>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.griffith.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-design-1189',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '020086A';
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>This Honours program has been designed to enable students who have demonstrated substantial ability at an undergraduate level to develop advanced levels of studio practice, supporting theory and an advanced level of research understanding.</p><p>While studying Design (Honours), you''ll have the ability to choose a project or topic that you''re passionate about and have the space and access to studios, software and equipment to explore that further.</p><h5>Graduate outcomes</h5><p>Our design graduates will have unprecedented opportunity to contribute and lead in vital new forms of social and economic development. Designers work across a range of fields roles, including interior design, product and service design and graphic design as well as interactive and 4D design.<h5>Tailor your timetable</h5><p>Even if you study full-time on-campus, you may still be able to customise your degree to suit your needs. From a range of tutorial times to online access to lectures and other course material, we''re here to help you fit study in with your work and life commitments.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 52,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 38500,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<p>The University''s <a href="https://sharepointpubstor.blob.core.windows.net/policylibrary-prod/Admission%20Policy.pdf">Admission Policy</a> will apply.</p><p><strong>Note:</strong> Applicants are permitted to defer an offer subject to availability of supervisors upon recommencement. </p><p>To be eligible for admission to this Honours program, consideration will be given to the following criteria:</p><ul><li>A GPA of at least 5.0 (credit level) over the second and third year of the Bachelor degree;*</li><li>have achieved a GPA of at least 5.0 in the major studio components of the second and third years of the undergraduate degree</li><li>have completed 30 credit points in theory in the second and third years of the undergraduate degree with a GPA of at least 5.0</li><li>A suitable Research Proposal (please see questions in the <a href="https://www.griffith.edu.au/__data/assets/pdf_file/0024/1661514/Honours-Admissions-Guide-2023-V3.pdf" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">QCAD Undergraduate Honours Admissions Guide</a> ) and the resources available to support the candidature. This proposal should include a portfolio containing images of relevant work and demonstrate a strong and sustained studio practice (please see criteria in the <a href="https://www.griffith.edu.au/__data/assets/pdf_file/0024/1661514/Honours-Admissions-Guide-2023-V3.pdf" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">QCAD Undergraduate Honours Admissions Guide</a> ).</li><li>The availability of an appropriate proposed supervisor. The confirmation of your Supervisor will be approved upon entry into the program. At times, where the nominated Supervisor is no longer able to supervise the project, a suitable Supervisor with be allocated by the Honours Program Director. The link to full-time staff members who may act as Supervisors is available here: <a href="https://www.griffith.edu.au/arts-education-law/queensland-college-art-design/staff" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Queensland College of Art and Design Staff</a> </li><li>The preparedness of the applicant to undertake the degree in terms of the elapsed time since the prospective candidate qualified for the award of a Bachelor degree and the academic preparation provided by the Bachelor''s degree for the candidate''s proposed Dissertation topic.</li><li>[*] Bachelor of Design program or equivalent studies.</li></ul><h5>Inherent requirements</h5><p>Inherent requirements are the essential components of a program or course that demonstrate the abilities, knowledge and skills required to achieve the core learning outcomes of the course or unit.&nbsp;</p><p>Inherent requirements for this program are identified&nbsp;<a href="https://www.griffith.edu.au/__data/assets/pdf_file/0016/2225014/Inherent-Requirements_Bachelor-of-Design_Honours.pdf" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">here</a>.</p>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.griffith.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-design--honours-2043',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '029377F';
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p><strong>The Brisbane South (Nathan) offering of this program is scheduled to be delivered at the Treasury Building at our Brisbane City campus in 2027. If scheduled opening is delayed, courses may be delivered all or in part at our other Brisbane locations.</strong></p><p>Our Bachelor of Digital Marketing and Analytics prepares you to thrive in a world where AI, automation and data-driven decision-making are reshaping how brands connect with people. You''ll learn to blend creativity with analytics, understand what drives consumer behaviour and design marketing strategies that cut through in an increasingly digital world. You''ll gain the digital marketing and analytics skills that today''s employers demand.&nbsp;</p><p>Griffith is among the top 1% of business schools worldwide accredited by both the International Association to Advance Collegiate Schools of Business (AACSB) and the European Foundation for Management Development Quality Improvement System (EQUIS). Your qualification carries global recognition and reflects our commitment to delivering a future-focused business education.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Highlights of studying the Bachelor of Digital Marketing and Analytics&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>Learn to use data-driven insights to solve real business problems, identify opportunities and improve performance across industries.&nbsp;</li><li>Build strong foundations in marketing, advertising and consumer behaviour while exploring how AI, analytics and digital technologies are transforming the industry.&nbsp;</li><li>Tailor your degree with electives that match your interests, whether you''re drawn to social media strategy, UX, branding, data storytelling or emerging tech.&nbsp;</li><li>Gain practical, job-ready capabilities through hands-on projects, industry tools and authentic marketing challenges.&nbsp;</li><li>Study within a supportive cohort and take part in programs like BusinessPLUS, with sustainability and responsible business practices embedded throughout your learning.&nbsp;</li></ul><p>Throughout your degree, you''ll develop the future-ready analytical, strategic and creative skills needed to succeed in digital marketing roles shaped by rapid technological change. You''ll learn how to gather and interpret data, understand audiences on a deeper level and design campaigns that respond to real-time trends. With AI now influencing everything from content creation to predictive analytics, you''ll graduate confident in your ability to work alongside advanced technologies.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Queensland''s #1 university for AI.</strong> (ShanghaiRanking''s Global Ranking of Academic Subjects 2025)</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 156,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 111000,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Academic entry requirements (by country)</h4><p>Academic entry requirements apply to International applicants for this program. You can view the academic entry requirements for this program <a href="" data-target="#intlEntryModal" data-toggle="modal">here</a>.</p>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.griffith.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-digital-marketing-and-analytics-1691',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '120962G';
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p><strong>This degree is pending dual accreditation with the Queensland College of Teachers (QCT) and the Australian Children''s Education &amp; Care Quality Authority (ACECQA). </strong></p><p>Everyone has that one teacher that always believed in them. Be that teacher for your students and help create a brighter future for the next generation.</p><p>This degree is designed to meet the urgent need for high-quality teachers in early childhood centres and primary schools and other educational settings.</p><h6>Highlights of studying the Bachelor of Early Childhood and Primary Education</h6><ul><li>A shared foundation year, between the Bachelor of Early Childhood and Primary Education, Bachelor of Primary Education and Bachelor of Secondary Education, to develop key insights into major trends and themes in education. This shared foundation year allows for a seamless transition between degrees, giving you time to decide which age group you feel most comfortable teaching.</li><li>Benefit from our strong relationships with schools and industry partners. During your studies, you''ll undertake 110 days of supervised professional experience with a dedicated placement officer to assist in organising your placement.</li><li>Choose to specialise in a range of in-demand areas, including early childhood, STEM and digital technologies, to boost your teaching career early.</li><li>Learn at your own pace, with flexible options including online learning you may be able to fast-track your studies.</li><li>Once the degree is accredited, accredited, eligible students can apply for Queensland teacher registration as soon as they graduate.</li></ul><p>Teacher education at Griffith University has a focus on wellbeing and inclusive education, ensuring you enter the classroom with the skills to make a difference.</p><p>In line with our belief that education should be for everyone, you''ll develop strategies and resources to prepare you to teach learners from diverse academic and personal backgrounds. Throughout your studies, you''ll develop your curriculum planning skills and build your confidence to design, deliver and evaluate lessons to ensure you graduate as an experienced and capable educator.</p><h6>Meet your mathematics prerequisite</h6><p>Ready to study a teaching degree but don''t have the mathematics prerequisite? Successfully completing <a href="https://www.griffith.edu.au/apply/admission-pathways/bridging-and-enabling-programs/bridging-maths" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Griffith''s Bridging Maths for Aspiring Educators</a> course will meet your subject requirements for entry into our education degree and you could start your studies in the next available trimester. This course is delivered over six weeks in on-campus and online modes.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 208,
    offshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Academic entry requirements (by country)</h4><p>Academic entry requirements apply to International applicants for this program. You can view the academic entry requirements for this program <a href="" data-target="#intlEntryModal" data-toggle="modal">here</a>.</p><p>Note: Successful completion of the Literacy and Numeracy Test for Initial Teacher Education (LANTITE) is not an entry requirement for this program. However, if you have achieved a ''satisfactory'' result for one or more component of the Literacy and Numeracy Test for Initial Teacher Education (LANTITE) at another institution, the ''satisfactory'' result can be carried across with your program application. You are not eligible to apply for a place in the program if one or more component of LANTITE remains at ''unsatisfactory'' after two test attempts for that component. Griffith University does not support reset of LANTITE test attempts.</p><p><strong>Inherent requirements</strong></p><p>Inherent requirements are the essential components of a program or course that demonstrate the abilities, knowledge and skills required to achieve the core learning outcomes of the course or unit.</p><p>Inherent requirements for this program are identified <a href="https://www.griffith.edu.au/__data/assets/pdf_file/0021/2235333/2027_BEarlyChildPrimEdu_Inherent-Requirements.pdf" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">here</a>.</p>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.griffith.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-early-childhood-and-primary-education-1722',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '120232H';
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>Everyone has that one teacher that always believed in them. Be that teacher for your students and help create a brighter future for the next generation.</p><h6>Highlights of Studying the Bachelor of Education&nbsp;</h6><ul><li>Benefit from our strong relationships with schools and industry partners. During your studies, you will undertake 80 days of supervised professional experience and we have a dedicated placement officer to assist in organising your placement.&nbsp;</li><li>Choose to specialise in a range of in-demand areas, including early childhood, STEAM and digital technologies, to give your career a kick-start.&nbsp;</li><li>Learn at your own pace, with flexible options and accelerated modes to fast-track your studies.</li><li>This degree is accredited by the Queensland College of Teachers (with early childhood recognised by ACEQA), allowing eligible applicants to apply for Queensland teachers registration as soon as they graduate.&nbsp;</li></ul><p>Teacher education at Griffith University has a focus on wellbeing and inclusive education, ensuring you enter the classroom with the skills to make a difference. Your studies will follow one of the below paths:</p><ul><li><strong>Bachelor of Education (Primary Education &amp; Early Childhood Education)</strong></li><li><strong>Bachelor of Education (Primary Education)</strong></li><li><strong>Bachelor of Education (Secondary Education)</strong></li></ul><p>In line with our belief that education should be for everyone, you''ll develop strategies and resources to prepare you to teach learners from diverse academic and personal backgrounds. Throughout your studies, you will hone your curriculum planning skills and build your confidence to design, deliver and evaluate lessons to ensure you graduate as an experienced and capable educator.</p><h6>Bachelor of Education (Primary Education)</h6><p>Our primary education curriculum covers areas such as history and geography, the way language develops and works, mathematics, science and technology, health and physical education, and the arts. You can also choose to specialise in Early Childhood Education, Health and Physical Education, Special Needs Education, English, Mathematics or Science.&nbsp;</p><h6>Bachelor of Education (Secondary Education)</h6><p>You''ll learn the knowledge and skills to teach students through years 7 to 12 and can choose to undertake studies in two teaching areas, or the Learning Support major and one teaching area. We offer a large range of Secondary Education teaching areas, including:&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Biology</li><li>Chemistry^</li><li>Design Technology</li><li>Digital Technologies</li><li>Drama</li><li>English</li><li>Food and Nutrition</li><li>Geography</li><li>Health and Physical Education</li><li>History</li><li>Mathematics</li><li>Physics</li><li>Psychology</li><li>Visual Arts.</li></ul><p>For teaching area content offered online, ensure you review course information for the most current and accurate details regarding online and on-campus attendance.</p><p><em>^ When selecting Chemistry, your other teaching area must be Biology, Mathematics or Food and Nutrition.</em></p>',
    course_duration_per_week = NULL,
    offshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Academic entry requirements (by country)</h4><p>Academic entry requirements apply to International applicants for this program. You can view the academic entry requirements for this program <a href="" data-target="#intlEntryModal" data-toggle="modal">here</a>.</p><p>Note: Successful completion of the Literacy and Numeracy Test for Initial Teacher Education (LANTITE) is not an entry requirement for this program. However, if you have achieved a ''satisfactory'' result for one or more component of the Literacy and Numeracy Test for Initial Teacher Education (LANTITE) at another institution, the ''satisfactory'' result can be carried across with your program application. You are not eligible to apply for a place in the program if one or more component of LANTITE remains at ''unsatisfactory'' after two test attempts for that component. Griffith University does not support reset of LANTITE test attempts.</p><h5>Inherent requirements</h5><p>Inherent requirements are the essential components of a program or course that demonstrate the abilities, knowledge and skills required to achieve the core learning outcomes of the course or unit.</p><p>Inherent requirements for this program are identified here .</p>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.griffith.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-education-1567',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '090883C';
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>Get hands-on experience solving real industry problems to build a better tomorrow today. Immerse yourself in an engineering hub with a dedicated building, flexible learning styles and smaller classes where you''ll receive personalised attention from teachers invested in your success. At Griffith, you''ll learn by doing, gaining the hands-on experience and industry connections that employers value most. You''ll also have the chance to join active clubs and societies that connect you with like-minded peers and expand your professional community.</p><p>During your study, you''ll engage in extensive industry placements, collaborative projects and hands-on research opportunities. With a wide choice of majors, strong professional networks and intentionally smaller cohorts, you''ll graduate with the confidence, skills and connections to step straight into your career.</p><h6>Specialisations tailored to your passion&nbsp;</h6><p>Whether you''re drawn to designing infrastructure, working with renewable energy, or advancing cutting-edge tech like drones and robotics, you''ll find a specialisation that lets you follow your passion and make an impact.&nbsp;</p><p>Choose from a wide range of engineering majors, including:&nbsp;</p><ul><li><strong>Civil Engineering</strong>&nbsp;(Gold Coast, Brisbane South (Nathan))</li><li><strong>Electrical and Electronic Engineering</strong>&nbsp;(Gold Coast)</li><li><strong>Electrical and Renewable Energy Engineering</strong>&nbsp;(Gold Coast)</li><li><strong>Electronic Engineering</strong>&nbsp;(Brisbane South (Nathan))</li><li><strong>Electronic and Energy Engineering</strong>&nbsp;(Brisbane South (Nathan))</li><li><strong>Environmental Engineering</strong>&nbsp;(Gold Coast, Brisbane South (Nathan))</li><li><strong>Mechanical Engineering</strong>&nbsp;(Gold Coast, Brisbane South (Nathan))</li><li><strong>Mechatronics&nbsp;</strong>(Gold Coast, Brisbane South (Nathan))</li></ul><p><a href="https://www.griffith.edu.au/griffith-sciences/school-engineering-built-environment/learning-teaching/engineering-majors" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Explore our majors in more detail.</a> </p><h6>Highlights of studying the Bachelor of Engineering (Honours)&nbsp;</h6><ul><li>This degree is internationally accredited by Engineers Australia, ensuring your qualifications will be recognised worldwide through the Washington Accord.</li><li>Learn by solving real engineering problems, applying theory through practical, hands-on projects.</li><li>Build strong networks through industry placements, student clubs and active engineering communities.</li><li>Choose from a wide variety of engineering majors to match your career ambitions.</li><li>Gain extensive experience through research, collaborative projects and professional mentoring.&nbsp;</li><li>Graduate highly employable with strong technical expertise, practical experience and industry connections.&nbsp;</li></ul><h6>Industry experience and global opportunities&nbsp;</h6><p>In your final year, complete a trimester-long capstone project through the Industry Affiliates Program. Apply your skills to genuine engineering challenges locally or overseas, gaining more than 400 hours of professional experience and building your career network. You may also take part in an international field trip, further expanding your global perspective.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 208,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 182000,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Academic entry requirements (by country)</h4><p>Academic entry requirements apply to International applicants for this program. You can view the academic entry requirements for this program <a href="" data-target="#intlEntryModal" data-toggle="modal">here</a>.</p>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.griffith.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-engineering--honours-1546',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '090583D';
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p><strong>Queensland''s #1 university for marine and ocean engineering.</strong> (ShanghaiRanking''s Global Ranking of Academic Subjects 2025)</p><p>Study environmental science at Griffith and gain the scientific knowledge, practical experience and confidence to tackle some of the most pressing challenges of our time. This degree blends strong scientific foundations with hands-on learning, preparing you for a career where you can make a genuine impact on the environment and society.</p><p>Whether your goal is to better understand natural systems or actively protect them, you''ll graduate with skills, scientific rigour and informed decision-making expertise in environmental management. At Griffith, you''ll learn in a living lab as our campuses are surrounded by bushland, waterways and marine ecosystems, giving you direct exposure to real environmental systems with sustainability and environmental responsibility embedded throughout your studies.</p><p>You''ll explore environmental challenges from social, physical and biological perspectives, supported by an interdisciplinary curriculum spanning ecology, chemistry, data science, management and policy. Learning takes place well beyond the classroom, with extensive fieldwork, lab activities and immersive field trips in unique natural environments.</p><h6>Highlights of studying the Bachelor of Environmental Science</h6><ul><li>With more than 50 years'' experience training environmental scientists, Griffith understands industry and government needs, ensuring you graduate career-ready.</li><li>Gain extensive hands-on experience through labs, ecological surveys, data modelling, applied research, field trips and professional placements with government, NGOs and industry partners.</li><li>Learn the tools and technologies used by industry, aligning your skills with employer expectations and easing the transition into the workforce.</li><li>Study in living lab environments across our campuses and complete an unforgettable capstone research experience on Heron Island.</li><li>With supportive lecturers, tailored academic support and strong industry and research connections, you''ll feel supported every step of the way as you build the career-ready skills employers value.</li><li>The degree''s accreditation with the Environment Institute of Australia and New Zealand (EIANZ) enhances employability, professional recognition and access to exclusive opportunities.</li></ul><h6>Build strong foundations and graduate career-ready&nbsp;</h6><p>Your degree begins with core science courses before progressing into environmental data analytics, geographical information systems, management and anthropology. In your final year, you''ll complete a capstone experience, choosing from a research project, extended fieldwork or an industry placement-allowing you to apply your learning to real environmental problems.</p><h5>Majors&nbsp;</h5><p>Flexible study options mean you can complete a double major and still graduate in three years. Choose from a range of majors to tailor your degree and align your studies with your career goals:</p><p><strong>Ecology and Conservation</strong> - explore ecosystems, biodiversity and conservation science through practical ecological surveys and monitoring. Available at Gold Coast and Brisbane South (Nathan).</p><p><strong>Environmental Chemistry</strong> - investigate the chemical processes that shape natural systems and pollutants, with advanced lab and analytical skills. Available at Gold Coast and Brisbane South (Nathan).</p><p><strong>Soil and Water Science</strong> - study the management of Australia''s critical soil and water resources through fieldwork, catchment studies and ecology. Available at Brisbane South (Nathan) only.</p><p><strong>Urban and Social Environments</strong> - examine the relationship between people, cities and nature, with a focus on sustainability, planning and community engagement. Available at Gold Coast and Brisbane South (Nathan).</p><h6>Honours&nbsp;</h6><p>From the end of your third year, eligible students can transfer into an honours program and complete an independent research project, strengthening pathways into research, leadership roles or further study.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 156,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 129000,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Academic entry requirements (by country)</h4><p>Academic entry requirements apply to International applicants for this program. You can view the academic entry requirements for this program <a href="" data-target="#intlEntryModal" data-toggle="modal">here</a>.</p>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.griffith.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-environmental-science-1547',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '090584C';
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>Develop expertise in physical, biomedical, and psychological sciences to launch your career in exercise science. Learn the role of exercise in health maintenance and rehabilitation and how it can be applied to create interventions that improve health, fitness, wellbeing and performance. </p><h6>Highlights of studying the Bachelor of Exercise Science </h6><ul><li>Study courses in anatomy, physiology, psychology, biomechanics, nutrition and more. </li><li>Learn how the body moves and how to assess human performance through exercise. </li><li>Build skills to boost performance, prevent injuries, manage health risks and promote the benefits of exercise. </li><li>Gain experience through placements in our on-campus clinics, or with big names like Swimming Australia, Gold Coast Titans and Queensland Academy of Sport. </li><li>Graduate ready for careers in sport, health, fitness and rehab, or continue into further study like physiotherapy or clinical physiology. </li></ul><h6>Learn to lead in collaborative care </h6><p>The best outcomes for patients and health professionals rely on a collaborative, inclusive approach to health. At Griffith, we prepare you for the future of healthcare by learning alongside students and staff from the full range of clinical areas, building crucial skills for multidisciplinary teams. </p><h6>The Gold Coast''s home of health </h6><p>Griffith Health has a major presence within the Gold Coast Health and Knowledge Precinct, across the road from the Gold Coast University Hospital. Our state-of-the-art labs provide an unrivalled learning experience, including our $150 million Griffith Health Centre, immersive virtual learning environment, and on-site professional clinics for student placements in allied health, occupational and physical therapy labs for practical experience. </p><p>Placements may also be available in Northern NSW Tweed Valley Hospital, offering the latest state-of-the-art learning and teaching hub for hands-on experience.</p><h5>Honours</h5><p>The <a href=''../Search/Results?SearchText=2096''>Bachelor of Exercise Science (Honours) (2096)</a> is available as an additional year of study for high-achieving students.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 156,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 124500,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Academic entry requirements (by country)</h4><p>Academic entry requirements apply to International applicants for this program. You can view the academic entry requirements for this program <a href="" data-target="#intlEntryModal" data-toggle="modal">here</a>.</p>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.griffith.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-exercise-science-1171',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '017687B';
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>This program is designed to provide students with an opportunity to undertake advanced study and supervised research work in the specialisation defined by their undergraduate degree program within the context of a multidisciplinary cohort.</p> <p>The research skills developed within this program will provide an attractive credential for students seeking employment in the public or private sectors. The program will also provide the necessary preparation for entry into a higher degree research program. The multidisciplinary context of the program, involving team-teaching of students and the sharing of coursework and seminar experiences across disciplines will be invaluable to students given the importance of a multidisciplinary approach to researchers and practitioners seeking to understand complex problems in health.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 52,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 41500,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<p>The University''s <strong>Bachelor Honours Degree (AQF Level 8) Policy</strong> will apply.<p> <p>The criteria for admission to this Honours program are:</p> <ul> <li>successful completion of the Griffith Bachelor of Exercise Science or an equivalent qualification from another university and</li> <li>a <abbr title="Grade Point Average">GPA</abbr> of at least 5.0 over the second and third year of the Bachelor degree.</li> </ul> <p>The Program Director will take the following into consideration when assessing applications for admission:</p> <ul> <li>the suitability of the proposed dissertation topic, the resources available to support the candidature and the availability of appropriate supervision and</li> <li>the preparedness of the applicant to undertake the degree in terms of the elapsed time since the prospective candidate qualified for the award of a Bachelor degree and the academic preparation provided by the Bachelor degree for the candidate''s proposed dissertation topic.</li> </ul><p><strong>Note:</strong> Applicants are permitted to defer an offer subject to availability of supervisors upon recommencement. </p>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.griffith.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-exercise-science--honours-2096',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '081364A';
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p><strong>From Trimester 1 2027,</strong>&nbsp;the primary pathway for admission to the Bachelor of Film and Screen Media Production is via ATAR/Rank.</p><p>Applicants who achieve an&nbsp;<strong>ATAR/Rank of 75.00 (or higher) are guaranteed admission</strong>&nbsp;into the program for 2027. ATAR/Rank Guarantees apply until the main offer round in December and/or until places are filled.</p><p>Develop your skills as an innovative content creator with access to state-of-the-art facilities, strong industry connections and embedded engagement opportunities. In the Bachelor of Film and Screen Media Production, you''ll learn to collaborate in teams to bring your vision to life, while building a solid foundation in film history, practice, critical analysis and emerging technologies like virtual production.</p><p>This hands-on, production-focused degree provides the skills, knowledge and studio experience to thrive in a dynamic, competitive and constantly evolving field.</p><h6>Highlights of studying the Bachelor of Film and Screen Media Production</h6><ul><li>Learn by doing in our on-campus film production facilities, with access to high-end, industry-grade digital cinema cameras and dollies, LED lighting and sound recording equipment.</li><li>Develop your skills and your own vision alongside a cohort of inspired, collaborative Griffith Film School students from a range of creative disciplines.</li><li>Showcase your work in film festivals and awards and collaborate with animators and game designers from Griffith Film School, creatives from the Queensland College of Art and Design and musicians from Queensland Conservatorium.</li><li>Take your creativity on the road, with the option to undertake various domestic and international study tours.</li></ul><h6>Create in facilities designed for the future of film</h6><p>Work on sound stage, multi-camera, motion capture and virtual production projects. Complete them in our post-production suites and recording studios, then host viewings in our own 95-seat cinema.</p><h6>Industry focus</h6><p>Take advantage of our workshop, seminar and master class programs delivered by local and international experts.</p><p>Griffith Film School is an active member of, and has a strong reputation within, the World Film School Association (CILECT), a group of 160 International Film Schools, as well as other international partners including:</p><ul><li>APSA</li><li>NEP Group</li><li>World Congress of Science and Factual Producers</li><li>Gobelins L''école De L''image</li><li>BFA.</li></ul><p>These industry links and international connections mean you''ll have the opportunity to practise the art of filmmaking under the guidance of the best in the world and make critical contacts that you''ll draw upon at university and beyond.</p><h5>Majors</h5><h6>Film production</h6><p>Prepare for the modern production landscape by developing advanced skills in cameras, lighting, sound and editing tools, enabling you to transform scripts into captivating visual narratives.</p><h6>Streaming television</h6><p>Gain experience in the dynamic landscape of digital streaming and television. You''ll learn how to leverage various platforms, analyse industry trends and audiences, and develop content, while refining your skills in single and multi-camera studio and location productions.</p><h6>Writing and development</h6><p>Write and develop ideas for any screen medium, from linear screenplays to narrative design.</p><h6>Virtual production and VFX</h6><p>Discover how to create content through innovative virtual production methods, including motion capture, LED wall technology, photogrammetry, camera tracking and virtual lighting through real-time game engines.</p><h6>3D art and environments</h6><p>Learn to interpret visual concepts and artistic styles to create appealing 3D characters, props, vehicles, and environments for games, film and animation.</p><h6>Post-production</h6><p>Develop skills in the creative application of advanced compositing techniques including animated typography, motion graphics and green screen concepts, as well as mastering compositing workflows, colour correction and node-based compositing tools.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 156,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 112500,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h5>Portfolio requirements</h5><p>International applicants are required to submit a portfolio together with their application for this program and further admission information is available in the following brochure:</p><ul><li><a href="https://www.griffith.edu.au/__data/assets/pdf_file/0016/2103361/GFS-INT-Portfolio-Reqs-2025-v3.pdf" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Portfolio Requirements for International Applicants</a></li></ul><h4>Academic entry requirements (by country)</h4><p>Academic entry requirements apply to International applicants for this program. You can view the academic entry requirements for this program <a href="" data-target="#intlEntryModal" data-toggle="modal">here</a>.</p>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.griffith.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-film-and-screen-media-production-1284',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '058710B';
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>Unlock your potential in the world of forensic science, where rigorous scientific training underpins real-world criminal investigation. Our Bachelor of Forensic Science is Queensland''s only dedicated and accredited forensic science degree, designed to give you the crime scene, laboratory and investigative skills trusted by employers. With a strong science-first approach and a focus on practical learning, you''ll graduate as a confident, job-ready forensic professional.</p><p>You''ll build strong foundations in chemistry and biology before applying them to forensic contexts - a critical advantage in a field where scientific accuracy matters. Study alongside a supportive student community, learn from approachable academics with real case experience, and connect directly with industry through guest lectures, networking events and professional bodies such as the Australian and New Zealand Forensic Science Society (ANZFSS). You''ll gain a clear understanding of what forensic careers really involve and the multiple pathways available beyond traditional roles.</p><h6>Highlights of studying the Bachelor of Forensic Science</h6><ul><li>Study Queensland''s only accredited forensic science degree, developed to meet industry standards and employer expectations.</li><li>Build strong chemistry and biology foundations through a science-first curriculum, before applying your skills to forensic investigation.</li><li>Develop the practical lab and analytical skills employers demand through extensive hands-on experience in forensic biology and chemistry.</li><li>Learn to evaluate evidence objectively, using contemporary forensic analysis methods and emerging investigative technologies.</li><li>Learn from industry-leading academics who have provided expert evidence in Australian courts.</li><li>Gain experience through casework, reporting and moot court simulations.</li><li>Engage with the forensic profession through ANZFSS events, guest talks from police and private forensic labs and dedicated student careers evenings.</li></ul><h6>Hands-on experience in forensic investigation</h6><p>From your first year, you''ll develop a deep understanding of forensic investigation grounded in hard science. You''ll study core courses in biology, chemistry, molecular genetics and forensic investigation before progressing into your chosen major. In second and third year, you''ll refine your expertise through advanced lab work and applied forensic analysis, building a comprehensive, industry-relevant skillset.</p><h6>Double your opportunities</h6><p>The <a href=''../Search/Results?SearchText=1706''>Bachelor of Forensic Science/Bachelor of Criminology and Criminal Justice (1706)</a> double degree is also available. Combine forensic science with criminology to strengthen your understanding of legal and criminal justice systems and broaden your career opportunities across forensic investigation, regulation and law enforcement.</p><h5>Forensic science majors</h5><p><strong>Forensic Chemistry: </strong>Apply chemistry to real-world investigations using industry-aligned analytical techniques. You''ll gain experience across organic, inorganic, physical and analytical chemistry, working with cutting-edge instrumentation to analyse substances and trace evidence. With applications in toxicology, drug analysis and environmental forensics, this major prepares you for roles as a forensic chemist, toxicologist or analytical scientist. Royal Australian Chemical Institute (RACI) accreditation for this major signals standards-aligned training and enhances graduate credibility with employers.</p><p><strong>Forensic Molecular Biology:</strong> Combine genetics and justice through advanced molecular and cellular techniques used in human identification and criminal investigation. You''ll study DNA profiling, gene expression, protein science and molecular biology, gaining extensive lab experience through forensic applications. Graduates are prepared for roles such as forensic biologist, DNA analyst or molecular laboratory scientist.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 156,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 129000,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Academic entry requirements (by country)</h4><p>Academic entry requirements apply to International applicants for this program. You can view the academic entry requirements for this program <a href="" data-target="#intlEntryModal" data-toggle="modal">here</a>.</p>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.griffith.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-forensic-science-1264',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '049312B';
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>The games industry is growing and evolving at an extraordinary rate. This degree is designed to equip you with the complex skills you''ll need for a successful career conceptualising and creating the next wave of games and virtual worlds.</p><h6>Highlights of studying the Bachelor of Game Design and Production</h6><ul><li>Work individually and in teams on projects that meet commercial standards, collaborating with multidisciplinary creatives with a wide range of production skills and expertise.</li><li>Access an exciting calendar of exhibitions, guest lectures and masterclasses.</li><li>Learn from some of the country''s leading designers, who are already pushing the boundaries of game design and creative arts.</li><li>Connect with designers, filmmakers, animators, illustrators and musicians across Griffith''s various creative schools.</li><li>Engage with practitioners and gain hands-on experience working on game design projects for real clients through our commercial multimedia production arm, LiveLab.</li></ul><h6>Build your network and skills&nbsp;</h6><p>Develop vital contacts and networks through our local and global industry links with leading organisations like Epic Games, Toon Boom, Liquid Animation, Animal Logic, NEP, Asia Pacific Screen Academy, Ludo (Bluey) and Cutting Edge.</p><h6>Become part of the industry</h6><p>Griffith University is an official Unreal Academic Partner, giving you access to the powerful Unreal Engine used for high-fidelity games and virtual production. We are also a member of the Interactive Games and Entertainment Association (IGEA), connecting you with the games industry across Australia and New Zealand.</p><h5>Majors</h5><p>You''ll choose a specialisation, while also having the freedom to explore contemporary developments in the practice of interactive game design and related disciplines. Gain essential knowledge and studio experience in areas like:</p><p><strong>Virtual production and VFX: </strong>Discover how to create engaging, dynamic content with virtual production and its innovative methods, including motion capture, LED wall technology, photogrammetry, camera tracking and virtual lighting through real-time game engines. You''ll learn to use these tools to produce immersive, visually striking worlds that blend physical and digital elements seamlessly, so you can take part in revolutionising how we create and experience media.</p><p><strong>3D art and environments: </strong>Learn to interpret visual concepts and artistic styles to create appealing 3D characters, props, vehicles and environments for games, film and animation. Using industry-standard tools and cutting-edge technology, you''ll develop skills in modelling, texturing, lighting, and rendering to create assets that inspire and immerse. This area of study combines artistry with technical precision, giving you the ability to craft visually compelling experiences that resonate with audiences on an emotional and narrative level.</p><p><strong>Gameplay programming: </strong>Through practical, hands-on projects, you''ll build a strong foundation in the technical side of game development, becoming proficient in programming and software design. You''ll learn to work with industry-standard coding languages and master game engine mechanics to create innovative and engaging experiences. Areas of study include game architecture, AI programming, and multiplayer functionality, giving you the tools to design systems that are both efficient and exciting to play.</p><p><strong>Art direction:</strong> Learn how to shape the overall vision of a project and ensure every detail supports its creative impact. In this major, you''ll learn advanced techniques in conceptualisation, visual storytelling and art direction principles to guide the look and feel of characters, environments and story-worlds. You''ll explore how to develop cohesive styles, create strong visual identities, and communicate artistic intent effectively across animation, games and screen media.</p><p><strong>Character animation:</strong> Develop advanced skills in rigging, keyframe animation and motion capture integration to create characters that move, emote and interact convincingly. You''ll explore the subtle details of timing, weight and expression that make animated performances connect with audiences across games, films and digital media. By blending technical expertise with artistic sensitivity, you''ll learn how to craft characters that feel real and relatable, driving storytelling and immersing viewers in dynamic, emotional experiences across a wide range of platforms and genres.</p><p><strong>Writing and development: </strong>Learn how to write compelling stories, scripts and interactive narratives that capture audience attention and imagination. You''ll explore techniques for building authentic characters, dynamic dialogue and engaging worlds, while also understanding how different media and platforms shape storytelling approaches. Alongside creative practice, you''ll gain insights into the global screen industry, audience trends and professional pathways.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 156,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 115500,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h5>Portfolio requirements</h5><p>International applicants are required to submit a portfolio together with their application for this program and further admission information is available in the following brochure:</p><ul><li><a href="https://www.griffith.edu.au/__data/assets/pdf_file/0016/2103361/GFS-INT-Portfolio-Reqs-2025-v3.pdf" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Portfolio Requirements for International Applicants</a> </li></ul><p><strong>Inherent requirements</strong></p><p>Inherent requirements are the essential components of a program or course that demonstrate the abilities, knowledge and skills required to achieve the core learning outcomes of the course or unit.</p><p>Inherent requirements for this program are identified&nbsp;<a href="https://www.griffith.edu.au/__data/assets/pdf_file/0025/2220748/B-Game-Design-and-Prod_Inherent-Requirements.pdf" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">here</a>.</p><h4>Academic entry requirements (by country)</h4><p>Academic entry requirements apply to International applicants for this program. You can view the academic entry requirements for this program <a href="" data-target="#intlEntryModal" data-toggle="modal">here</a>.</p>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.griffith.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-game-design-and-production-1697',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '115557G';
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>This program is designed to provide students with an opportunity to undertake advanced study and supervised research work in Public Health within the context of a multidisciplinary cohort. The scope of Public Health is inclusive of a broad range of specialties in many health related disciplines.</p><p>The research skills developed within this program will provide an attractive credential for students seeking employment in the public or private sectors. The program will also provide the necessary preparation for entry into a higher degree research program. The multidisciplinary context of the program, involving team-teaching of students and the sharing of coursework and seminar experiences across disciplines will be invaluable to students given the importance of a multidisciplinary approach to researchers and practitioners seeking to understand complex problems in health.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 52,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 36000,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<p>The University''s <a href="https://sharepointpubstor.blob.core.windows.net/policylibrary-prod/Admission%20Policy.pdf">Admission Policy</a> will apply.</p><p>The criteria for admission to this Honours program are:</p><ul> <li>successful completion of an undergraduate degree in any health discipline from Griffith or another university and</li> <li>a <acronym title="Grade Point Average">GPA</acronym> of at least 5.0 over the second and third year of the Bachelor degree.</li></ul><p>The Program Director will take the following into consideration when assessing applications for admission:</p><ul> <li>the suitability of the proposed dissertation topic and</li> <li>the resources available to support the candidature and the availability of appropriate supervision and</li> <li>the preparedness of the applicant to undertake the degree in terms of the elapsed time since the prospective candidate qualified for the award of a Bachelor degree and the academic preparation provided by the Bachelor degree for the candidate''s proposed dissertation topic.</li></ul><p><strong>Note:</strong> Applicants are permitted to defer an offer subject to availability of supervisors upon recommencement. </p>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.griffith.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-health--honours--in-public-health-2121',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '096709B';
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>Empower communities and transform lives through health knowledge. Health science provides an understanding of the human body and the science underpinning being a health practitioner. This degree provides a high level of flexibility with a range of majors leading to many rewarding career paths.</p><p>With five-star ratings for skills development, student support and teaching quality*, you''ll be equipped to take advantage of a growing job market or further health specialisation.</p><h6>Highlights of studying the Bachelor of Health Science</h6><ul><li>In your first year, explore health issues and build a solid foundation in human biology including chemistry, cell biology, anatomy, physiology, genetics, microbiology, health management, nutrition, infection and toxicology.</li><li>Expand your knowledge in years two and three, refining your skills in analysis, evaluation, and communication.&nbsp;</li><li>Tailor your studies by selecting a major, as well as a wide range of electives.</li><li>Take advantage of our connections for industry placements and practical experience.</li></ul><h6>Industry connections and experience</h6><p>The BioHealth Projects capstone course provides an authentic learning experience, working directly with industry partners on real projects. As a final-year Health Science student, you''ll apply your knowledge to solve practical problems, while building valuable connections for your future career.</p><p>You''ll gain practical experience, develop your problem-solving and project management skills, and receive mentorship from both industry professionals and Griffith staff. It''s a great opportunity to showcase your skills, enhance your CV, and work on projects that could lead to future job opportunities. As part of a diverse cohort, you''ll bring together expertise across a range of health science fields. Make an impact, expand your professional network and prepare for a successful career in health and biosciences.</p><h6>Study Health Science in immersive environments&nbsp;</h6><p>Learn in state-of-the-art facilities, with immersive simulated teaching environments, virtual reality technology and clinical labs. We''ve invested in world-class research, facilities and some of Australia''s most highly awarded academics. When you choose to study health science at Griffith, you''re joining a forward-thinking, future-ready university that shares your passion for making a difference that matters.</p><p>*Good Universities Guide (2024)</p><h5>Majors</h5><p><strong>Data Management and Analytics: </strong>Gain the skills to transform complex health data into meaningful insights. You''ll learn to collect, process, visualise and analyse data from sources such as electronic records and social media, using modern analytics tools to support evidence-based decision-making in health environments.</p><p><strong>Health Communication: </strong>Learn how to effectively communicate complex health and science information to diverse audiences across a range of platforms. With a focus on media relations, ethical and legal frameworks, crisis communication and global storytelling, you''ll develop the practical and strategic skills needed to influence public understanding and support informed decision-making.</p><p><strong>Pharmaceutical Science: </strong>Build a strong foundation in the science of drug action, formulation and delivery, combining key principles from chemistry, biology and pharmacology. Learn how medicines are developed, how they interact with the body and how they are safely and effectively delivered.</p><h5>Honours</h5><p>The <a href=''../Search/Results?SearchText=2101''>Bachelor of Health Science (Honours) (2101)</a> is available as an additional year of study.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 156,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 123000,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Academic entry requirements (by country)</h4><p>Academic entry requirements apply to International applicants for this program. You can view the academic entry requirements for this program <a href="" data-target="#intlEntryModal" data-toggle="modal">here</a>.</p>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.griffith.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-health-science-1093',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '017585G';
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h5>Advance your expertise with an Honours degree in multidisciplinary health research</h5><p>Take your studies to the next level with advanced coursework and supervised research in your chosen health specialisation. With five-star ratings from The Good Universities Guide (2024) for overall experience, engagement, skills development, student support and teaching quality, you''ll be ready to capitalise on a growing job market or enhance your research skills for future opportunities.</p><h6>Highlights of studying the Bachelor of Health Science (Honours)</h6><ul><li>An Honours degree can strengthen your application for competitive clinical programs by developing critical research skills, demonstrating academic excellence, and providing opportunities for publications, networking, and deeper knowledge in a relevant field. </li><li>Through team-based learning and shared experiences across disciplines, you''ll gain a deeper understanding of complex health issues. </li><li>Working alongside a multidisciplinary cohort, you''ll develop valuable research skills that will make you stand out to employers in both the public and private sectors. </li><li>Your Honours studies will serve as a strong foundation to pursue further research studies.&nbsp;</li><li>Completion of this degree will better prepare you for a successful career in health research. </li></ul>',
    course_duration_per_week = 52,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 41000,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<p>The University''s <a href="https://sharepointpubstor.blob.core.windows.net/policylibrary-prod/Admission%20Policy.pdf" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Admission Policy</a> will apply.</p><p>The criteria for admission to this Honours program are:</p><ul><li>successful completion of the Griffith Bachelor of Health Science or an equivalent qualification from another university and</li><li>a Grade Point Average (GPA) of at least 5.0 over the second and third year of the Bachelor degree.</li></ul><p>The Program Director will take the following into consideration when assessing applications for admission:</p><ul><li>the suitability of the proposed dissertation topic, the resources available to support the candidature and the availability of appropriate supervision and</li><li>the preparedness of the applicant to undertake the degree in terms of the elapsed time since the prospective candidate qualified for the award of a Bachelor degree and the academic preparation provided by the Bachelor degree for the candidate''s proposed dissertation topic.</li></ul><p><strong>Note:</strong> Applicants are permitted to defer an offer subject to availability of supervisors upon recommencement. </p>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.griffith.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-health-science--honours-2101',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '081371B';
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>Make a real difference in your community. This degree prepares you to work with individuals, families and communities to help overcome challenges in areas such as health, housing, education, employment, disability or social connection. Use your skills to support and connect people and the resources they need, and work to make systems easier to navigate and more supportive.</p><h6>Highlights of studying the Bachelor of Human Services&nbsp;</h6><ul><li>Explore human services in Australia and build a strong foundation in social justice, empowerment and inclusion to help shape a brighter future for those you work with.&nbsp;</li><li>Explore courses in human development, communication and counselling, social justice and diversity, ethics and case management.&nbsp;</li><li>Learn from specialists tackling issues such as youth mental health, parenting and family support, while gaining hands-on human services experience.&nbsp;</li><li>Career advice and support is built into your degree, so you''ll graduate job ready.&nbsp;</li></ul><h6>Practical experience that sets you apart&nbsp;</h6><p>Put your skills into practice through clinical placements in our on-campus clinics or with leading organisations like Queensland Health, Queensland Government, headspace and Lifeline.</p><h6>Combine classroom learning with hands-on training&nbsp;</h6><p>Guided by experienced professionals, you''ll complete 52 days of field placement across your second and third years. With opportunities in areas such as child protection, family support, mental health, youth justice, homelessness, domestic violence and disability and the option to take local, rural or international placements, you''ll graduate ready to make a real impact.</p><h5>Majors&nbsp;</h5><p>You''ll select a major in:</p><h6>Children, youth and family&nbsp;</h6><p>Support the wellbeing of children, young people and families through early intervention, advocacy and integrated service delivery. You''ll explore childhood development, family dynamics and youth needs in diverse social and cultural contexts, with a strong focus on safety, equity and care. Courses cover child development, youth services and family violence, equipping you with practical tools to work in early years settings, community programs and family support services. You''ll have the opportunity to undertake a supervised field placement, offering practical experience to build your confidence and professional capacity.</p><h6>Criminal justice&nbsp;</h6><p>Explore the structures, practices and challenges within the criminal justice system, with a focus on rehabilitation, crime prevention and justice reform. You''ll examine key areas such as corrections, restorative justice and responses to crime in diverse communities, including First Nations peoples. Gain practical experience through a supervised field placement, developing skills for roles in policy, community safety, youth justice or offender rehabilitation. With courses covering crime prevention strategies, lived experiences of justice and alternatives to traditional punishment, you''ll be well-positioned to make a difference to how justice is delivered and experienced in society.</p><h6>Disability, wellbeing and ageing&nbsp;</h6><p>Explore how individuals experience disability, ageing and mental health, with a strong focus on dignity, rights and inclusion. You''ll examine contemporary approaches to disability practice, positive ageing and mental wellbeing, learning from both lived experiences and critical perspectives. Through a supervised field placement, you''ll build the skills needed to work across diverse support settings, from aged care and disability services to mental health and community programs.</p><h6>Policy, advocacy and research&nbsp;</h6><p>Prepare to drive social change by influencing policy, shaping services and advocating for equity and justice. Gain foundational knowledge in welfare systems, government and legislation, alongside practical research and data analysis skills. With a focus on leadership, advocacy, and critical thinking, you''ll explore how to design evidence-informed interventions and influence decision-making at local and national levels. A supervised field placement allows you to apply your learning in policy and community settings.</p><h6><strong>Honours</strong></h6><p>The <a href=''../Search/Results?SearchText=2092''>Bachelor of Human Services (Honours) (2092)</a> is available through an additional year of study.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 156,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 106500,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Academic entry requirements (by country)</h4><p>Academic entry requirements apply to International applicants for this program. You can view the academic entry requirements for this program <a href="" data-target="#intlEntryModal" data-toggle="modal">here</a>.</p>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.griffith.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-human-services-1394',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '026703K';
