WHERE cricos_course_code = '081363B';
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>Join one of Australia''s leading music schools and develop the skills to become a versatile and creative musician, ready to make your mark and enter professional life. In the Bachelor of Music, you''ll explore your chosen specialisation while being immersed in diverse styles including classical, contemporary, jazz, popular, electronic, experimental and world music.</p><h6>Highlights of studying the Bachelor of Music </h6><ul><li>Audition for multiple instruments or specialisations and grow your skills across different musical and creative areas. </li><li>From your first year, you''ll refine your artistry through performance, collaboration and critical listening, laying the groundwork to succeed in the evolving music industry.</li><li>Explore diverse styles and choose majors from your second year: performance, contemporary creative practices, production and entrepreneurship, or community education. </li><li>Further develop your artistry through expert mentorship, studio training and live performance opportunities across multiple genres.</li></ul><h6>Discover your potential at Queensland Conservatorium&nbsp;</h6><p>Study at Queensland Conservatorium Griffith University and discover your artistic identity in a welcoming and supportive environment. You''ll learn from award-winning educators, perform alongside peers in ensembles and cross-genre projects and gain practical experience through internships, music industry collaborations and project-based studies.</p><p>With access to world-class facilities and global alumni networks, you''ll be well positioned to transition seamlessly into a career in music, continue into further study or a graduate entry teacher preparation program.</p><h5>Majors</h5><h6>Performance </h6><p>Grow as an artist and professional by developing advanced skills in classical, contemporary and/or jazz performance. This major has a strong focus on high performance levels, effective collaboration with peers and the expression of a distinct artistic identity.</p><h6>Contemporary creative practices </h6><p>Incorporating elements of composition, creative music technology and popular music, you''ll have the opportunity to create original music as a composer, digital practitioner, songwriter and/or sound artist. You''ll also gain a strong grounding in the role of computing in modern music-making.</p><h6>Production and entrepreneurship </h6><p>Collaborate with students from diverse disciplines, including musicians, singers, performers, composers, engineers and producers, to bring works to life, whether on the stage, film, online or live.</p><h6>Community education and leadership </h6><p>Build the skills and frameworks to teach and lead participatory music-making in a variety of community and educational settings. You''ll develop your leadership and teaching abilities and explore the practical, theoretical and ethical implications of working across social groups in schools, hospitals, prisons, cultural centres and more.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 156,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 123000,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Academic entry requirements (by country)</h4><p>Academic entry requirements apply to International applicants for this program. You can view the academic entry requirements for this program <a href="" data-target="#intlEntryModal" data-toggle="modal">here</a>.</p><p><strong>Audition requirements</strong></p><p>International applicants are required to submit and pass an Audition.&nbsp;Please submit your audition with your application for this program. Further admission audition information is available on the <a href="https://www.griffith.edu.au/arts-education-law/queensland-conservatorium/auditions/music" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Audition requirements website</a>.</p><h5>Inherent requirements</h5><p>Inherent requirements are the essential components of a program or course that demonstrate the abilities, knowledge and skills required to achieve the core learning outcomes of the course or unit.&nbsp;</p><p>Inherent requirements for this program are identified <a href="https://www.griffith.edu.au/__data/assets/pdf_file/0022/2230429/Inherent-Requirements-1687-Bachelor-of-Music.pdf" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">here</a>.</p>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.griffith.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-music-1687',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '081380A';
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>The Bachelor of Music (Honours) is a one-year Bachelor Honours degree available to students after graduating with the three-year Bachelor of Music.</p><p>The Bachelor of Music (Honours) degree aims to produce graduates who are highly skilled, musically adaptable and equipped to enter further Higher Degree by Research (HDR) study and/or professional life as creative and flexible 21st century musical performers and researchers. This program will provide the opportunity for students to develop their specialist interests through focus on a program of research or of practice-based work or a combination of both.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 52,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 41000,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<p>To be eligible for admission to this Honours program, a student will be expected to meet the following requirements:</p><ul><li>have successfully completed the requirements of a Bachelor of Music or hold a three or four year degree in music from a recognised university which is equivalent to the Bachelor of Music at Griffith University;</li><li>have achieved a minimum cumulative Grade Point Average (GPA) of 5.2 (on a scale of 7.0) or equivalent from a recognised University (consideration will be given to students who achieve a minimum Grade Point Average (GPA) of 5.2 in the final year of their program);</li><li>for those applying for the written research pathway provide a Dissertation Research proposal (maximum 1200 words) which outlines a rationale, research question and methodology and which demonstrates a sound understanding of relevant literature.&nbsp;</li><li>for those pursuing the artistic practice pathway, provide an artistic statement outlining the rational for applying for the BMus Honours, clearly outlining creative and professional aspirations (Max 500 words).&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong style="color: rgb(51, 51, 51);">Note:</strong>&nbsp;Applicants should complete the proforma that can be found <a href="https://www.griffith.edu.au/__data/assets/pdf_file/0034/2047984/Application-for-the-Bachelor-of-Music-Hons-2025.pdf" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">here</a> and submit it together with their application.</p><p><strong>Note:</strong> Applicants are permitted to defer an offer subject to availability of supervisors upon recommencement and audition if required. </p>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.griffith.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-music--honours-2051',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '076297E';
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>Take your musical theatre talent to the next level at one of Australia''s leading universities for performing artists. Studying musical theatre will see you undertake many facets of training to enter professional life as a creative, highly skilled and musically adaptable performer. Gain access to world-class training, professional-grade performance opportunities and a network of industry experts.</p><h6>Highlights of studying the Bachelor of Musical Theatre&nbsp;</h6><ul><li>Receive intensive practical training in acting, improvisation, speech, voice, singing, dance and movement.</li><li>Learn different musical theatre styles and key skills like music theory, aural awareness and ensemble work.</li><li>Develop your abilities to become a versatile and authentic performer who excels both as a collaborative company member and in the individual skills of singing, dancing and acting.</li><li>Gain authentic performance experiences in professional-standard productions.&nbsp;</li></ul><h6>World-class musical theatre training&nbsp;</h6><p>In partnership with the Queensland Performing Arts Centre (QPAC), our Queensland Academy of Excellence in Musical Theatre (QAEMT) offers unparalleled professional experience, purpose-built studios and training with the industry''s best.</p><h6>Discover your creative voice&nbsp;</h6><p>Our teaching blends classroom learning with real industry experience, giving you the freedom to explore and develop your own creative identity. You''ll gain hands-on training both on-stage and behind the scenes, working alongside skilled performers, creatives and industry professionals in a supportive, inclusive environment.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 156,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 115500,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Academic entry requirements (by country)</h4><p>Academic entry requirements apply to International applicants for this program. You can view the academic entry requirements for this program <a href="" data-target="#intlEntryModal" data-toggle="modal">here</a>.</p><p>Applicants are required to attend an audition where their abilities in singing, acting and dance are assessed. While no prior formal music theory studies are mandated, familiarity with at least basic music theory will be beneficial.</p><p>Admission to this program may also require applicants to meet any <strong>other eligibility requirements</strong>.</p><p><strong>Other</strong> <strong>eligibility requirements may include:</strong> Any applicable<strong> </strong>Prerequisites and/or Assumed Knowledge, English Language Proficiency and Minimum Age requirements.</p><p>Refer to ''QTAC and UAC requirements'' for any Prerequisites and/or Assumed Knowledge, ''Language Requirements'' section should you not have completed your secondary schooling or recent studies in Australia, Minimum Age requirements are detailed in the Admission Policy.</p><p><h4>Inherent requirements</h4><p>Inherent requirements are the essential components of a program or course that demonstrate the abilities, knowledge and skills required to achieve the core learning outcomes of the course or unit. </p><p>Inherent requirements for this program are identified <a href="https://www.griffith.edu.au/__data/assets/pdf_file/0029/1705295/B-Musical-Theatre-Inherent-Requirements.pdf" target="_blank"> here </a>.</p></p>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.griffith.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-musical-theatre-1404',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '082401D';
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p><strong>Australia''s #1 university for nursing and midwifery. </strong>(ShanghaiRanking''s Global Ranking of Academic Subjects 2025)</p><p><strong style="background-color: inherit;">The standard program (3 year) is available in Trimester 1 only.</strong></p><p><strong style="background-color: inherit;">Advanced standing (2 year) pathway is available in Trimester 1 &amp; 2.</strong></p><p>Gain the skills to become a confident and capable Registered Nurse. Experience world-class learning with workshops, online classes and diverse clinical placements to prepare you to make a real difference in the healthcare sector.</p><p>Nursing is the science of professional caring and offers opportunities to promote and restore health, prevent illness and alleviate suffering. You''ll learn how to make critical decisions, coordinate care and educate patients. Through diverse clinical placements, you will develop advanced healthcare, advocacy and leadership skills.</p><h6>Highlights of studying the Bachelor of Nursing</h6><ul><li>Future-proof your skills through the latest technology and teaching approaches.</li><li>Study in our on-campus simulation nursing wards and high-tech labs.</li><li>Take part in interactive workshops, simulated practice, online learning and varied clinical placements.</li><li>Learn alongside students and staff from the full range of clinical areas, preparing you to work across communities as part of a multidisciplinary team.</li><li>Enhance your skills through evidence-based care, focusing on nursing as a profession, while gaining exposure to various nursing specialties and receiving integrated employment support.</li><li>We produce the highest-quality graduates in the profession, supported by our culture of excellence in teaching, research and clinical practice.</li></ul><h6>Exciting clinical placements from the get-go</h6><p>Undertake work-integrated clinical placements with a difference. Choose from a range of placements in rural, remote and overseas locations and be supported by our expert team of practising professionals.</p><h6>Honours</h6><p>The <a href=''../Search/Results?SearchText=2094''>Bachelor of Nursing (Honours) (2094)</a> is available as an additional year of study.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 156,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 124500,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Academic entry requirements (by country)</h4><p>Academic entry requirements apply to International applicants for this program. You can view the academic entry requirements for this program <a href="" data-target="#intlEntryModal" data-toggle="modal">here</a>.</p><p>You can complete this program in 3 or 2 years depending on your prior study and work experience</p><p><strong style="background-color: inherit;">Standard Program 3 year duration (240CP) - </strong>Trimester 1 intake only</p><p><strong style="background-color: inherit;">Advanced Standing 2 year duration (160CP) - </strong>Trimester 1 and 2 intake</p><p>To be eligible you must meet one of the following criteria:</p><ul><li><strong>Enrolled Nurse </strong>with <strong>registration</strong>, generally with the Australian Health Practitioner Regulation Agency (Ahpra) (Division 2, unconditional (without restrictions)) and a <strong>Diploma of Nursing</strong> from an accredited Australian Education Provider</li><li><strong>Internationally qualified nurse </strong>and provide evidence of your international qualification, evidence of <strong>recency of practice</strong> and have unconditional <strong>registration </strong>where you are working as a Registered Nurse</li><li>a Griffith College<strong> Diploma of Health Care</strong></li></ul><p><strong style="background-color: inherit;"></strong></p><p><strong>Internationally qualified nurse - Recency of practice: </strong>We follow Nursing and Midwifery Board of Australia (NMBA) guidelines regarding recency of practice. You must have a minimum of 450 hours accumulated over the past five years. The hours do not need to be continuous.</p>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.griffith.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-nursing-1162',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '002436M';
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>To be awarded a Bachelor of Nursing (Honours) degree, one additional year of study is required following the successful completion of the Bachelor of Nursing.</p> <p>Graduates of Griffith University''s Bachelor of Nursing (Honours) degree have a competitive edge as they are equipped with practical skills, experience and attributes that employers value, coupled with highly developed research capabilities. </p><p>Offered by Griffith University''s <a href="https://www.griffith.edu.au/griffith-health/school-nursing-midwifery">School of Nursing and Midwifery</a>, our Bachelor of Nursing (Honours) will give you an opportunity to undertake advanced study and supervised research work.</p><p>You''ll complete coursework and a research preparation course in your first trimester and complete a dissertation in your second trimester. </p><p><strong>Coursework </strong><br> Through the 30-credit point coursework component of the Honours program, you''ll gain an understanding of how to critically evaluate research. You''ll also develop your knowledge of statistical analysis techniques as applied to scientific research and gain an awareness of how research proposals should be designed. </p> <p><strong>Dissertation</strong><br> Through the 50-credit point dissertation component, you''ll conduct research on a specific project and complete a seminar and dissertation describing the research in detail.</p> <p>You will be required to find a suitable supervisor for your research project prior to submitting your application for admission into the honours program. If you are unable to find a suitable supervisor, you',
    course_duration_per_week = 52,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 41500,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<p>The criteria for admission to this Honours program are:</p><ul><li>successful completion of a Bachelor of Nursing or an equivalent qualification and</li><li>a Grade Point Average (GPA) of at least 5.0 over the second and third years of the Bachelor degree.</li></ul><p>The Program Director will take the following into consideration when assessing applications for admission:</p><ul><li>the suitability of the proposed dissertation topic, the resources available to support the candidature and the availability of appropriate supervision and</li><li>the preparedness of the applicant to undertake the degree in terms of the elapsed time since the prospective candidate qualified for the award of a Bachelor degree and the academic preparation provided by the Bachelor degree for the candidate''s proposed dissertation topic.</li></ul><p><strong>Note:</strong> Applicants are permitted to defer an offer subject to availability of supervisors upon recommencement. </p>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.griffith.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-nursing--honours-2094',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '081361D';
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>Gain the skills to become an accredited dietitian and nutritionist, helping individuals and communities improve their health and wellbeing. Study dietetics to become a trusted expert in nutrition, providing evidence-based, personalised care across a variety of roles for people of all ages and health goals.</p><p>This degree provides the flexibility to advance your professional practice skills or to complete a dissertation in your final year of study.</p><h6>Highlights of studying the Bachelor of Nutrition and Dietetics (Honours)&nbsp;</h6><ul><li>Learn the science behind the body and food, including chemistry, anatomy, physiology and biochemistry.</li><li>As you progress, you''ll dive into advanced studies in nutrition and dietetics.</li><li>In Australia, all dietitians are nutritionists, but only dietitians can provide medical nutritional therapy to individual patients. Graduates of this degree will hold both qualifications.</li><li>Join a supportive student community with peer mentors and career advisers to help you succeed.</li></ul><h6>Gain experience with industry experts&nbsp;&nbsp;</h6><p>Learn through experience in state-of-the-art facilities, including a purpose-built teaching kitchen and a nutrition clinic at the Griffith Health Centre. You''ll be guided by Accredited Practising Dietitians with strong industry connections and supported throughout your degree, benefiting from Griffith''s five-star rated teaching, student support and resources*.</p><h6>Professional placements&nbsp;</h6><p>In the final stage of your degree, you''ll complete over 20 weeks (100+ days) of full-time professional placements across Queensland and/or interstate. You''ll put your skills into practice, build valuable industry connections, and work alongside future doctors, nurses, physiotherapists and other health professionals in advanced simulated clinical settings.</p><p><em>* Good Universities Guide 2025</em></p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 208,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 174000,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Academic entry requirements (by country)</h4><p>Academic entry requirements apply to International applicants for this program. You can view the academic entry requirements for this program <a href="" data-target="#intlEntryModal" data-toggle="modal">here</a>.</p><p><strong style="background-color: inherit;"> <a href=''../Search/Results?SearchText=1355''>Bachelor of Nutrition and Dietetics (1355)</a> Students </strong></p><p>Current <a href=''../Search/Results?SearchText=1355''>Bachelor of Nutrition and Dietetics (1355)</a> students that have completed Years 1, 2 and 3 are eligible to apply for admission to this program. Eligible students, as determined by the Program Director and subject to the following criteria, in this program will undertake the dissertation in Year 4,:</p><ul><li>achievement of a minimum Grade Point Average (GPA) of 5.0 for all coursework at the completion of third year/trimester one of <a href=''../Search/Results?SearchText=1355''>Bachelor of Nutrition and Dietetics (1355)</a>.</li></ul><p>The Program Director will take the following into consideration when assessing applications for admission:</p><ul><li>the suitability of the proposed dissertation topic; and</li><li>the resources available to support the candidature including availability of appropriate supervision.</li></ul>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.griffith.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-nutrition-and-dietetics--honours-1436',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '084289E';
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>Create a positive impact and deliver life-changing outcomes to people of all ages. Develop the expertise to help individuals, groups and communities participate in the everyday activities that matter most, whether recovering from illness or injury, adapting to disability, or overcoming barriers of marginalisation and exclusion.</p><p>You''ll gain a deep understanding of the science of health, behaviour and environments, learning how these combine to support participation and wellbeing. Through a mix of theory, practical training and diverse placements, you''ll develop the skills to enable people to live meaningful and fulfilling lives.</p><h6>Highlights of studying the Bachelor of Occupational Therapy (Honours)</h6><ul><li>Study human anatomy, psychology and sociology to understand how health impacts daily life.</li><li>Learn practical therapy skills, exploring rehabilitation, assistive technology and environmental modifications that support people at home, school, work and in the community.</li><li>Gain practical experience through placements in hospitals, community, disability and mental health settings.</li></ul><h6>Collaborate and connect</h6><p>Learn alongside students and staff across health disciplines, preparing you to work as part of a multidisciplinary team. This collaborative approach mirrors real-world practice and ensures you''ll graduate ready to make a difference in complex and dynamic healthcare environments.</p><h6>State-of-the-art facilities</h6><p>Study in learning spaces designed for practical training and immersive experiences. Our $150 million Griffith Health Centre, on-site clinics, occupational and physical therapy labs and virtual learning environments give you the tools and confidence to apply your skills in practice from day one.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 208,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 168000,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Academic entry requirements (by country)</h4><p>Academic entry requirements apply to International applicants for this program. You can view the academic entry requirements for this program <a href="" data-target="#intlEntryModal" data-toggle="modal">here</a>.</p>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.griffith.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-occupational-therapy--honours-1662',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '084288F';
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>Study the fast-paced, rewarding field of paramedicine, where you can make a real difference in people''s lives. This degree equips you with the essential skills and knowledge to work as a paramedic in traditional and non-traditional settings.</p><p>You''ll develop strong clinical decision-making, problem-solving and critical thinking skills, while gaining a deep understanding of the human body, paramedic practice and the care of diverse conditions, diseases and trauma.</p><h6>Highlights of studying the Bachelor of Paramedicine</h6><ul><li>Our small student intake means more personalised support, more opportunities for active participation and meaningful interaction and a closer connection with teaching staff.</li><li>Our simulation facilities give you authentic, hands-on clinical experience using the same equipment as the Queensland Ambulance Service and other paramedicine organisations in Australia and overseas.</li><li>Graduate prepared to confidently respond to a wide range of situations, helping to improve health and wellbeing.</li><li>Open doors to international opportunities, allowing you to work in different countries and grow your career in paramedicine.</li></ul><h6>Practical paramedicine experience&nbsp;</h6><p>Experience a variety of clinical placements that build your hands-on skills across different healthcare settings. You''ll complete ambulance placements-4 weeks at the end of your first and second years, and 6 weeks in your final year-on a four on, four off roster. Non-ambulance placements are also available, giving you a well-rounded understanding of healthcare challenges and helping you refine your professional practice.</p><h6>Honours</h6><p>The <a href=''../Search/Results?SearchText=2122''>Bachelor of Paramedicine (Honours) (2122)</a> is available through an additional year of study.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 156,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 129000,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Academic entry requirements (by country)</h4><p>Academic entry requirements apply to International applicants for this program. You can view the academic entry requirements for this program <a href="" data-target="#intlEntryModal" data-toggle="modal">here</a>.</p><p>Students who require a refresher or who have not done Year 12 Chemistry or Mathematical Methods are <strong>strongly recommended</strong> to undertake a bridging course prior to commencing this program. For further information, please visit our <a href="https://www.griffith.edu.au/apply/admission-pathways/bridging-and-enabling-programs" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Bridging and Enabling programs</a> and the <a href="https://www.griffith.edu.au/griffith-sciences/learning-teaching/science-short-courses" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Short courses</a> websites.</p>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.griffith.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-paramedicine-1533',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '094591E';
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>This program is designed to provide students with an opportunity to undertake advanced study and supervised research work in paramedic pre-hospital care.</p><p>The research skills developed within the program will provide an attractive credential for students seeking employment in the public or private sectors. The program will also provide the necessary preparation for entry into a higher degree research program. The multidisciplinary context of the program, involving team-teaching of students and the sharing of coursework and seminar experiences across disciplines will be invaluable to students given the importance of a multidisciplinary approach to researchers and practitioners seeking to understand complex problems in health.<strong> </strong></p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 52,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 43000,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<p>The University''s <a href="https://sharepointpubstor.blob.core.windows.net/policylibrary-prod/Admission%20Policy.pdf">Admission Policy</a> will apply.</p><p>The criteria for admission are:</p><ul> <li>successful completion of the Griffith <a href=''../Search/Results?SearchText=1533''>Bachelor of Paramedicine (1533)</a> or an equivalent qualification from another university;</li> <li>a Grade Point Average (GPA) of at least 5.0 over the second and third year of the Bachelor degree.</li></ul><p>The Program Director will take the following into consideration when assessing applications for admission:</p><ul> <li>the suitability of the proposed dissertation topic;</li> <li>the resources available to support the candidature including availability of appropriate supervision;</li> <li>the preparedness of the applicant to undertake the degree in terms of the elapsed time since the prospective candidate qualified for the award of a Bachelor degree and the academic preparation provided by the Bachelor degree for the candidate''s proposed dissertation topic.</li></ul><p><strong>Note:</strong> Applicants are permitted to defer an offer subject to availability of supervisors upon recommencement. </p>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.griffith.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-paramedicine--honours-2122',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '096710J';
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>Learn how medicines are developed, tested and used safely to improve lives and protect communities. This degree gives you the scientific expertise to understand how drugs and chemicals interact with the human body. With a strong focus on practical learning and real-world application, this degree prepares you for a career at the intersection of health, science and industry.</p><p>Through hands-on lab work and applied projects, you''ll build a deep understanding of pharmacology, toxicology and drug development, gaining insight into how safer and more effective treatments reach patients and communities.</p><h6>Highlights of studying the Bachelor of Pharmacology and Toxicology</h6><ul><li>Gain extensive experience in modern pharmacology, toxicology and analytical laboratories, developing practical skills valued by employers.</li><li>Learn from experts leading research in drug action, chemical toxicology, precision medicine and pharmaceutical science.</li><li>Build strong foundations in chemistry, biology, and anatomy before progressing into advanced studies of drug mechanisms, safety and efficacy.</li><li>Apply your learning to real challenges through project-based courses such as the BioHealth Project, working with industry, government or research partners.</li><li>Tailor your studies with electives that align with your interests across health, research, regulation or industry.&nbsp;</li></ul><h6>Practical learning with real impact&nbsp;</h6><p>From your first year, you''ll combine core health science courses with lab-based learning to understand how cells, tissues and organ systems respond to medicines and chemicals. As you progress, you''ll study drug action, toxic responses, pharmaceutical analysis and specialised delivery systems, gaining experience with industry-standard techniques such as spectroscopy, chromatography and molecular analysis. Courses in evidence-based practice, biostatistics and epidemiology will strengthen your ability to interpret data and support safe and effective medicine use.</p><p>In your final years, you''ll bring your skills together through applied research, industry-informed projects or an industry placement, building confidence, professional experience and career readiness.</p><h6>Build a strong foundation for further study</h6><p>This degree''s focus on pharmacology will provide you with an excellent foundation if you''re considering a degree in one of these areas:</p><ul><li>Pharmacy: <a href=''../Search/Results?SearchText=1614''>Bachelor of Pharmacy (Honours) (1614)</a> | <a href=''../Search/Results?SearchText=5661''>Master of Pharmacy (5661)</a></li><li>Medicine: <a href=''../Search/Results?SearchText=5099''>Doctor of Medicine (5099)</a></li><li>Dentistry: <a href=''../Search/Results?SearchText=1577''>Bachelor of Dental Health Science (1577)</a></li><li>Medical Research: <a href=''../Search/Results?SearchText=5763''>Master of Health and Medical Research (5763)</a></li></ul><h6>Extend your expertise with honours&nbsp;</h6><p>Eligible students can undertake an additional year of study in the <a href=''../Search/Results?SearchText=2118''>Bachelor of Pharmacology and Toxicology (Honours) (2118)</a>, completing an independent research project under academic supervision.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 156,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 124500,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Academic entry requirements (by country)</h4><p>Academic entry requirements apply to International applicants for this program. You can view the academic entry requirements for this program <a href="" data-target="#intlEntryModal" data-toggle="modal">here</a>.</p>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.griffith.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-pharmacology-and-toxicology-1528',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '087743G';
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>This program is designed to provide students with an opportunity to undertake advanced study and supervised research work in the specialisation defined by their undergraduate degree program within the context of a multidisciplinary cohort.</p><p>The research skills developed within this program will provide an attractive credential for students seeking employment in the public or private sectors. The program will also provide the necessary preparation for entry into a higher degree research program. The multidisciplinary context of the program, involving team-teaching of students and the sharing of coursework and seminar experiences across disciplines will be invaluable to students given the importance of a multidisciplinary approach to researchers and practitioners seeking to understand complex problems in health.</p><p>Pharmacy at Griffith is ranked #1 by the <a href="https://www.gooduniversitiesguide.com.au/university-ratings-rankings/2023/undergraduate/overall-experience/pharmacy" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Good Universities Guide 2023/24</a>&nbsp;for Overall Experience, Teaching Quality, and Student Support in Australia.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 52,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 41500,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<p>The University''s <strong>Bachelor Honours Degree (AQF Level 8) Policy</strong> will apply.<p><p>The criteria for admission to this Honours program are:</p><ul> <li>successful completion of the Griffith Bachelor of Pharmacology and Toxicology or an equivalent qualification from another university and</li> <li>a Grade Point Average (GPA) of at least 5.0 over the second and third year of the Bachelor degree.</li></ul><p>The Program Director will take the following into consideration when assessing applications for admission:</p><ul> <li>the suitability of the proposed dissertation topic, the resources available to support the candidature and the availability of appropriate supervision and</li> <li>the preparedness of the applicant to undertake the degree in terms of the elapsed time since the prospective candidate qualified for the award of a Bachelor degree and the academic preparation provided by the Bachelor degree for the candidate''s proposed dissertation topic.</li></ul></p></p><p><strong>Note:</strong> Applicants are permitted to defer an offer subject to availability of supervisors upon recommencement. </p>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.griffith.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-pharmacology-and-toxicology--honours-2118',
    updated_at = NOW()
