UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>Study with Queensland''s top-ranked university for criminology* and use your degree as a launch pad to join the fight for justice, contribute to a safer community and a better criminal justice system.</p><p>Learn from experts and industry leaders who bring their hands-on experience to your study. Our strong international research reputation means you will be taught by academics who are recognised worldwide in their various fields.</p><h6>Highlights of studying the Bachelor of Criminology and Criminal Justice</h6><ul><li>Explore the causes of crime, how laws are made and broken, the impacts on victims, offenders and the justice system''s response.</li><li>Analyse crime with a focus on social justice, including the roles of police, courts and corrections.</li><li>Draw on knowledge and insights from many fields of study including psychology, law, sociology, politics and social work.</li><li>Study topics like criminal law, homicide, First Nations justice, fraud and cybercrime, and domestic and family violence.</li><li>Learn how crime happens, ways it can be reduced and evidence-based strategies to keep communities safe. You''ll also explore how research is used to measure impact and improve understanding.</li><li>Develop practical skills in data analysis and visualisation to understand and interpret patterns and clearly present information. </li></ul><h6>Industry connections to build your future</h6><p>Engage in a wide variety of work-integrated learning experiences to help tackle issues faced by local communities. Our industry connections fuel our unique learning experiences to give you practical insight into the workings of the criminal justice system, as well as the opportunity to work with agencies matched to your career aspirations.</p><h6>Experience matters </h6><p>Join one of the largest communities of criminologists in the world and access the best minds in the industry. We''re internationally renowned for applied research that makes a difference and for close collaborations with practitioners and employers. That knowledge feeds into the most up-to-date study content, giving you the best skills for an employment edge.</p><p>You''ll develop career-ready skills and experience working on real projects, cumulating in a capstone course where you''ll work with industry on a project relating to a current local community crime problem. You''ll have the opportunity to apply for a professional placement experience throughout your degree and access one-on-one research mentoring by criminology experts through the Criminology Undergraduate Research Internship Program.</p><p><em>*#1 in Queensland, Law and Criminology, 2024 ShanghaiRanking Global Ranking of Academic Subjects</em></p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 156,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 114000,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Academic entry requirements (by country)</h4><p>Academic entry requirements apply to International applicants for this program. You can view the academic entry requirements for this program <a href="" data-target="#intlEntryModal" data-toggle="modal">here</a>.</p>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.griffith.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-criminology-and-criminal-justice-1112',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '061466E';
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p><strong>Queensland''s #1 university for law and criminology.</strong> (ShanghaiRanking''s Global Ranking of Academic Subjects 2025)</p><p>Study the Bachelor of Criminology and Criminal Justice online at your own pace and gain practical, career-focused skills to help prevent crime and shape better justice outcomes. Lead change, promote justice and build a safer society, all on your schedule.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>This flexible, fully online degree is designed to equip you with the insights, tools and industry knowledge to make a real impact in communities and criminal justice systems across Australia. You''ll explore the causes and consequences of crime, understand the experiences of victims and offenders, and examine how policing, courts and corrections respond to crime through a social justice lens. You''ll also gain hands-on experience through work-integrated learning opportunities and learn from internationally recognised researchers and industry professionals.&nbsp;</p><h6>Highlights of studying the Bachelor of Criminology and Criminal Justice&nbsp;</h6><ul><li>Study 100% online, on demand - designed to fit around your work and life.&nbsp;</li><li>Learn from world-renowned experts in fields like policing, domestic violence, youth justice, and cyber crime. Explore major topics including criminal law, homicide, First Nations justice, family violence, and fraud.&nbsp;</li><li>Build practical skills in crime prevention, research design, data analysis and policy evaluation.&nbsp;</li><li>Examine real issues using insights from psychology, sociology, politics, social work and law.&nbsp;</li><li>Participate in work-integrated learning opportunities with justice agencies and community organisations matched to your career aspirations.&nbsp;</li><li>Benefit from dedicated academic support and interactive online learning tools to stay engaged and motivated.&nbsp;</li></ul><h6>Learning that prepares you to make an impact&nbsp;</h6><p>Our strong links with justice organisations mean you''ll learn how criminal justice systems really operate - from law enforcement to rehabilitation and prevention. Through hands-on projects, simulations and research activities, you''ll develop the skills to critically evaluate evidence, assess policy and recommend change. You''ll graduate with the practical and analytical expertise to contribute to safer communities and a fairer justice system.&nbsp;</p><h6>Learn from experts driving change in the justice sector&nbsp;</h6><p>Our teaching staff are leaders in their fields, bringing current research and front line experience into your virtual classroom. From examining cyber crime trends to improving support for vulnerable populations, Griffith researchers are shaping justice reform at local, national and global levels. Their insights and networks will help you understand the issues that matter and help you confidently step into professional roles that make a real difference.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>This degree is part of </strong><a href="https://www.griffith.edu.au/study/griffith-go" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><strong>Griffith GO</strong></a><strong>, our 100% online, on-demand degrees that let you start when you''re ready, study at your own pace and learn from anywhere.&nbsp;</strong></p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 156,
    offshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<p>Prerequisites: Nil</p><p>Assumed Knowledge:&nbsp;Any General or Applied English subject (Units 3 &amp; 4, C)</p><p>ATAR/Rank*: 63.00</p><p>VET Qualification: Certificate III</p><p>*The above ATAR/Rank from the 2026 admission cycle represents the minimum adjusted ATAR/Rank to which an offer was made. Minimum thresholds can change from year to year and should be used as a guide only for any future intakes.</p><p>The University''s <a href="https://sharepointpubstor.blob.core.windows.net/policylibrary-prod/Admission%20Policy.pdf">Admission Policy</a> will apply.</p>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.griffith.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-criminology-and-criminal-justice-1715',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '061466E';
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p><h3><strong>DEVELOP YOUR SKILLS FOR A LIFE AGAINST CRIME.</strong></h3> <p>The Bachelor of Criminology and Criminal Justice (Honours) is designed for students who want to hone their knowledge and skills through research. </p> <p>You''ll gain research training at a standard that will prepare you for postgraduate studies in justice administration, criminal justice or criminology. You''ll also learn about advanced theoretical concepts and policy debates in contemporary criminology - setting you up to access a career at more than an entry-level position in the criminal justice system. </p> <p>Your research will help to identify the social issues that lead to crime. You''ll also learn to understand what makes criminals tick as well as how to minimise the negative impacts of crime on society. </p> <h4>Industry and expert connections</h4> <p>At Griffith, criminology has always had a strong industry connection and a high level of cooperation from police agencies and other crime related bodies. This Honours degree continues the tradition with a multitude of opportunities to meet with and hear from industry experts. </p> <h4>Graduate outcomes</h4> <p>This degree sets you to enter the criminal justice system in a broader and usually higher range of rewarding roles such as an analyst or program design consultant - careers where the ability to do independent research is key. It also offers you a great pathway into a PhD, a Bachelor of Criminology and Criminal Justice (Honours) puts you one step ahead. </p></p><h4>Flexibility</h4> <p><strong>Tailor your timetable</strong> - Even if you study full-time on-campus, you may still be able to customise your degree to suit your needs. From a range of tutorial times to online access to lectures and other course material, we''re here to help you fit study in with your work and life commitments.</p><p><h4>Global mobility</h4> <p>This may be possible through a study abroad opportunity or through Criminology Student Society organised experiences with police and corrections. </p> <p>For more information on projects commencing from 2024 onwards please click on the following link: <a href="https://www.griffith.edu.au/__data/assets/pdf_file/0035/1780982/CCJ-Research-Project-Showcase-2024.pdf">CCJ Research Project Showcase 2024.pdf</a></p></p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 52,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 38000,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<p>The University''s <a href="https://sharepointpubstor.blob.core.windows.net/policylibrary-prod/Admission%20Policy.pdf">Admission Policy</a> will apply.</p><p>Applicants must have completed a Bachelor of Criminology and Criminal Justice or equivalent and have a minimum GPA of 5.0 in core second and third year courses AND must have completed Statistics (<a href=''/programs-courses/Course/2009CCJ''>2009CCJ Quantitative Methods for Social Research</a>) and Research Methods (<a href=''/programs-courses/Course/3012CCJ''>3012CCJ Criminology and Criminal Justice Research Methods</a>) and attained at least a grade of 5.0 in both these courses (or their equivalents).</p><p>For more information on projects commencing from 2024 onwards please click on the following link: <a href="https://www.griffith.edu.au/__data/assets/pdf_file/0035/1780982/CCJ-Research-Project-Showcase-2024.pdf" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">CCJ Research Project Showcase 2024.pdf</a></p><p><strong>Note:</strong> Applicants are permitted to defer an offer subject to availability of supervisors upon recommencement. </p>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.griffith.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-criminology-and-criminal-justice--honours-2117',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '062205G';
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p><strong>Queensland''s #1 university for AI.</strong> (ShanghaiRanking''s Global Ranking of Academic Subjects 2025)</p><p>Step into one of Australia''s fastest-growing and most in-demand fields with a Bachelor of Cyber Security. You''ll master the tools and technologies that protect critical data, systems and networks across business, government and everyday life. You''ll develop a deep understanding of how cyber-attacks occur and how to stop them, through practical training, real-world simulations and industry experience.</p><h6>Highlights of studying the Bachelor of Cyber Security</h6><ul><li>Train in cutting-edge facilities like our Cyber Range, a dedicated simulated environment where you''ll defend against live cyber incidents and test your skills in realistic scenarios.</li><li>Learn from industry experts who bring cyber security experience from sectors including government, finance and national defence.</li><li>Build a strong foundation in IT fundamentals including programming, networking, data management and systems administration, before diving into advanced cyber security topics.</li><li>Study with industry experts trusted by top financial institutions - including Westpac - to train their teams in combating financial crime.</li></ul><h6>Specialised, in-demand cyber expertise</h6><p>Study industry-relevant topics like ethical hacking, digital forensics, cryptography, cyber defence, incident response and AI, keeping you at the forefront of emerging technology and global security trends. Developing expertise in these areas is essential to protect organisations from complex, evolving cyber threats and to meet the growing demand for skilled professionals.</p><h6>Immerse yourself in the field before you graduate</h6><p>In your final year, you''ll gain valuable in-field experience through a professional industry placement or research project, preparing you for a confident transition to the workforce.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 156,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 121500,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Academic entry requirements (by country)</h4><p>Academic entry requirements apply to International applicants for this program. You can view the academic entry requirements for this program <a href="" data-target="#intlEntryModal" data-toggle="modal">here</a>.</p>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.griffith.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-cyber-security-1677',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '114026J';
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>Take your first step towards a rewarding career in dentistry. Develop a strong foundation in our cutting-edge health facilities and gain clinical experience with real patients as you build the skills to excel in this essential profession.</p><p>On successful completion of this degree, you''ll be eligible for entry to the <a href=''../Search/Results?SearchText=5703''>Master of Dentistry (5703)</a> to complete your training.</p><h6>Highlights of studying the Bachelor of Dental Health Science</h6><ul><li>Study the science behind the human body and oral health, including anatomy, physiology, biochemistry, pathology, and microbiology.</li><li>Develop practical dental skills, clinical techniques and professional practice knowledge right from your first year.</li><li>Learn from practising educators who have also led and contributed to globally significant research.</li><li>Our dedicated spaces for dental researchers make Griffith University the first choice for students studying dentistry and oral health.</li></ul><h6>Clinical training and experience with real patients&nbsp;</h6><ul><li>Gain experience in our state-of-the-art simulation labs before applying your skills in the Griffith Dental Clinic, where you''ll work alongside registered dentists and dental specialists. With 117 modern dental chairs and over 6,000 patient appointments each year, you''ll have extensive opportunities to develop your clinical expertise.</li></ul><h6>Honours</h6><p>The <a href=''../Search/Results?SearchText=2126''>Bachelor of Dental Health Science (Honours) (2126)</a> is available through an additional year of study for students who want to take their education to an advanced level and produce original research. It includes an additional one year of full-time study, or two years part-time, and offers a pathway to higher degree research. Honours is an attractive credential for potential employers.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 156,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 213000,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<p>The Bachelor of Dental Health Science is a quota-managed program as there are a limited number of places available to ensure sufficient resources are available to support the students.</p><p>In addition to the demonstration of English proficiency, admission to the Bachelor of Dental Health Science (for International students) will be determined by the following criteria:</p><h5><strong>1. University Clinical Aptitude test Australia/New Zealand (UCAT ANZ) </strong></h5><p>The UCAT ANZ assists universities to select applicants with the most appropriate abilities and professional behaviours required to become successful clinicians. To progress to the second component of the application process, all potential applicants must first complete this test.</p><p>*Dates and deadlines for 2025 UCAT ANZ will be published on <a href="https://www.ucat.edu.au/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">UCAT ANZ</a> in December.</p><h5><strong>2. Griffith University Dental Admissions Process Interviews (GUDAPs)</strong></h5><p>Applicants will be selected for the Griffith University Dental Admissions Process Interviews (GUDAPs) based on their UCAT ANZ Total Score. The GUDAPs will be conducted via SAMMI® (Scalable Automated Multiple Mini Interviews) using Sammi-Select software.&nbsp;Applicants will complete their interview at any time during the interview period by responding to a series of pre-recorded questions from Griffith University staff. The interviews will assess applicants'' suitability based on five factors:</p><ul><li>Motivation to study and work in Dentistry;</li><li>Teamwork skills;</li><li>Communication and empathy;</li><li>Ethics and social awareness; and</li><li>Critical thinking skills.</li></ul><h5><strong>3. Academic Attainment</strong></h5><ul><li>School leavers - academic achievements in Year 12 or equivalent; or University study - applicants who have undertaken at least one year full-time tertiary study or equivalent will have a rank depending on the duration and overall Grade Point Average (GPA) achieved.</li></ul><p>Each of the three components above are weighted and have a minimum threshold that must be met. Once all three weighted components are completed, scores will be combined and candidates will be ranked on their overall score. Completion of all components may not result in an applicant receiving an admission offer.</p><h4>Academic entry requirements (by country)</h4><p>Academic entry requirements apply to International applicants for this program. You can view the academic entry requirements for this program <a href="" data-target="#intlEntryModal" data-toggle="modal">here</a>.</p>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.griffith.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-dental-health-science-1577',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '094385M';
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>This program is designed to provide students with an opportunity to undertake advanced study and supervised research work in the specialisation defined by their undergraduate degree program within the context of a multidisciplinary cohort.</p><p>The research skills developed within this program will provide an attractive credential for students seeking employment in the public or private sectors. The program will also provide the necessary preparation for entry into a higher degree research program. The multidisciplinary context of the program, involving team-teaching of students and the sharing of coursework and seminar experiences across disciplines will be invaluable to students given the importance of a multidisciplinary approach to researchers and practitioners seeking to understand complex problems in health.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 52,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 71000,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<p>The criteria for admission to this Honours program are:</p><ul><li>successful completion of the Griffith Bachelor of Dental Health Science or Bachelor of Oral Health in Dental Science degree or an equivalent qualification from another university, and</li><li>a Grade Point Average (GPA) of at least 5.0 over the second and third year of the Bachelor degree. A candidate whose levels of achievement falls below this level may apply in writing for special consideration</li><li>the suitability of the proposed dissertation topic, the resources available to support the candidature and the availability of appropriate supervision, and </li><li>the preparedness of the applicant to undertake the degree in terms of the elapsed time since the prospective candidate qualified for the award of a Bachelor degree and the academic preparation provided by the Bachelor degree for the candidate''s proposed dissertation topic.</li></ul><p><strong>Note:</strong> Applicants are permitted to defer an offer subject to availability of supervisors upon recommencement. </p>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.griffith.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-dental-health-science--honours-2126',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '0101267';
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>Take your first steps towards becoming a registered dental hygienist. With the Bachelor of Dental Hygiene you''ll gain the ability to provide patient-centred oral health care, including assessment, diagnosis, treatment, management and education for the management and prevention of oral diseases in patients of all ages.</p><p>You''ll have the opportunity to undertake practical training in specialty clinics and learn from dental specialists in the fields of:&nbsp;</p><ul><li>periodontology&nbsp;</li><li>radiology and radiography&nbsp;</li><li>orthodontics&nbsp;</li><li>oral pathology&nbsp;</li><li>pharmacology&nbsp;</li><li>special needs&nbsp;</li><li>public health and health promotion.&nbsp;</li></ul><h6>Highlights of studying the Bachelor of Dental Hygiene</h6><ul><li>Learn to assess, diagnose, treat, manage, and educate patients in the prevention of oral diseases.&nbsp;</li><li>Hands-on training in specialty clinics in the disciplines periodontology, implantology and orthodontics&nbsp;</li><li>Learn skills in public health and health promotion to provide appropriate preventive oral health education to individuals and communities.</li></ul><h6>Clinical training in a collaborative environment</h6><p>Build practical skills in our state-of-the-art dental clinic and simulation lab, learning the latest techniques and technologies alongside dentistry students. You''ll also work with dentists, dental technicians, dental prosthetists and specialists, developing the communication and teamwork skills essential for effective patient care and clinical practice.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 156,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 135000,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<h4>Academic entry requirements (by country)</h4><p>Academic entry requirements apply to International applicants for this program. You can view the academic entry requirements for this program <a href="" data-target="#intlEntryModal" data-toggle="modal">here</a>.</p>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.griffith.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-dental-hygiene-1613',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '0100243';
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>Specialise in the rewarding field of dental prosthetics, learning to diagnose, design, manufacture and fit removable dentures. Through coursework and supervised clinical training, you''ll build the skills and experience needed to work directly with patients and collaborate across the wider dental team.</p><p>This degree is designed for qualified dental technicians ready to advance their career as an independent clinician. Graduates from Griffith''s Bachelor of Oral Health in Dental Technology or Bachelor of Dental Technology are encouraged to apply for this degree to gain a dental prosthetist qualification and may receive credit towards the degree.</p><p><strong><em>Note: </em></strong>The Bachelor of Dental Prosthetics is not available to those who hold or are studying towards a dentistry qualification.</p><h6>Highlights of studying the Bachelor of Dental Prosthetics</h6><ul><li>Develop advanced technical and clinical expertise to solve complex oral health challenges.</li><li>Gain extensive experience using the latest digital tools and technologies in dental prosthetics.</li><li>Learn from practising dental prosthetists and specialists in fields such as oral pathology, pharmacology, radiology and prosthodontics.</li><li>Collaborate with dentistry students in real clinical settings to strengthen your communication and teamwork skills.</li><li>Participate in team-based treatment planning to build confidence in patient care and referral processes.</li><li>Engage in the Team Based Treatment Planning Process to develop patient referral skills.</li></ul>',
    course_duration_per_week = 52,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 44500,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<p>To be eligible for admission to the <strong>Bachelor of Dental Prosthetics (Graduate Entry)</strong> program, a student must have:</p><ul><li>a Bachelor of Dental Technology degree (or equivalent) from Griffith University or a partner University, completed within the past ten years with a minimum GPA score of 4.00 (on Griffith University 7 point scale); <strong>OR</strong></li><li>Bachelor of Dental Technology degree awarded more than ten years ago and have been registered as a Dental Technician in Australia or New Zealand within ten years of the planned date of commencing the program.</li></ul><p>Note: This program is quota-managed for which there is a limited number of places available to ensure that sufficient resources are available to support the students. Meeting the admission requirements for this program may not result in an applicant receiving an admission offer.</p>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.griffith.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-dental-prosthetics-1638',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '102310D';
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>This degree equips you with the technical expertise and creative skill to design and manufacture custom-made dental devices that enhance oral health and function. Dental technologists (or dental technicians as they are often referred to) are highly skilled members of the dental team.</p><p>This is an ideal degree if you have an eye for detail and an artistic or scientific background. Graduates work behind the scenes to create and manufacture dentures, crowns, bridges and orthodontic appliances in both conventional and digital contexts.</p><h6>Highlights of studying the Bachelor of Dental Technology</h6><ul><li>Combine art and science to create custom-made dental devices that restore function and appearance.</li><li>Learn foundational health science and prosthetic principles, then progress to advanced dental laboratory techniques.</li><li>Gain experience with industry-standard CAD/CAM technology, including milling and 3D printing.</li><li>Work with a wide range of materials such as gold, porcelain, lost wax, and acrylic, and learn to record precise details like tooth colour and shape.</li><li>Study human anatomy in our Anatomy Lab with real specimens to deepen your understanding of dental and facial structures.</li></ul><h6>Work with advanced technology in professional settings&nbsp;&nbsp;</h6><p>Develop professional experience through practical work-integrated learning in your third year and placements in commercial dental laboratories. Learn alongside dentistry students in our world-class dental clinics featuring 117 modern chairs and over 6,000 patient appointments each year.</p><p>Whether your interests lie in the artistry of aesthetic design or the technical challenge of advanced dental materials and technologies, this degree offers a pathway to a rewarding and in-demand profession.</p><h5>Honours</h5><p>The <a href=''../Search/Results?SearchText=2127''>Bachelor of Dental Technology (Honours) (2127)</a> is available for students who want to advance their education through original research and deepen their expertise in dental technology.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 156,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 141000,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<p>Admission to the Bachelor of Dental Technology (for International students) will be determined by the following criteria:</p> <ul> <li>Academic achievement in Year 12 or equivalent. </li> <li>Demonstration of English proficiency. </li> </ul><h4>Academic entry requirements (by country)</h4><p>Academic entry requirements apply to International applicants for this program. You can view the academic entry requirements for this program <a href="" data-target="#intlEntryModal" data-toggle="modal">here</a>.</p>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.griffith.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-dental-technology-1574',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '094387J';
